            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-xxl",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-xl",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>You know that moment when your air purifier chimes and you pause: subscribe or buy filters in bulk? I get it. It's one of those decisions that feels like it should be simpler than it is. Let me walk you through what actually makes sense for your home, without the marketing noise.</p><p>The truth is, the \"better\" choice depends on your real life. Some households absolutely should subscribe. Others genuinely save money by buying in bulk. And some find a hybrid approach works best. Let's figure out which one makes sense for you.</p><h2>Air Filter Subscription Costs vs. Buying Filters in Bulk</h2><p>Here's the straightforward part: Blueair filter subscriptions typically offer 15-20% ongoing discounts plus 25% off your first filter. That's nice, but there's more to consider than just the price tag.</p><p>Take a<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/products/blue-pure-511i-max-1\"> Blue Pure 511i Max</a>: filters cost $29.99 individually. With filter subscription discounts and the 25% first-filter offer, costs become much more manageable over time. For a<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/products/blue-pure-211i-max-1\"> Blue Pure 211i Max</a>, individual filters are $69.99, a serious investment if buying multiple filters upfront.</p><p>The real issue: when you buy filters in bulk, you're betting your future needs stay exactly the same. If your life changes, new pets, relocation, growing family, developing allergies, your forecast fails, and you're stuck with excess inventory.</p><h2>Why Filter Replacement Subscriptions Work for Most Families</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "s3"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_KnqYBR": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
