            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-0",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "1096px",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/image1_7ce1dd74-19bb-4b68-887f-0f7d93630cd0.jpg",
            "image_desktop": "shopify://shop_images/image1_7ce1dd74-19bb-4b68-887f-0f7d93630cd0.jpg",
            "caption": "",
            "caption_style": "p6",
            "product": ""
          }
        },
        "text_e9yarP": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-lg",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-lg",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>A filter subscription lets you adjust whenever you need to. You can pause deliveries when traveling for weeks, skip a month if conditions improve, or resume whenever circumstances change. There's no waste, no locked-in commitment, and no guesswork about future needs.</p><h3>Multi-unit homes particularly benefit</h3><p>One consolidated bill, one automatic filter delivery schedule, one account to manage. Plus, if you upgrade units later, subscription filters always match your current equipment. You don't end up with incompatible filters wasting money.</p><h3>Life happens</h3><p>Pet adoption, family growth, moving to polluted areas, or new allergies all increase how often filters degrade. With automatic filter delivery flexibility, your costs align with reality, not guesses you made months ago.</p><h2>When Buying Air Purifier Filters in Bulk Makes Sense Instead</h2><p>If you have one<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/products/f3max-replacement-pac-filter-for-311i-max\"> Blue Pure 311i Max</a> in a completely stable situation with no pets, no expected changes, proper climate-controlled storage, buying 3 filters upfront (~$135) might save $12-42 over three years compared to filter replacement subscription costs.</p><p>But you've also locked in money and bet everything on predictions being perfect. What if conditions change? Your bulk inventory becomes a liability, and filters stored improperly may degrade faster than expected.</p><h2>Comparing Filter Types With Your Air Filter Replacement Strategy</h2><p>Blueair offers three filter options, each with different pricing and benefits:</p><p>Particle + Carbon (Standard) - $29.99 to $69.99</p><ul><li>Best for most households</li><li>Handles particles and basic odors</li><li>Most cost-effective choice</li><li>6-9 month lifespan</li></ul><p><a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/products/smokeblock-replacement-filter-for-211i-max\">SmokeBlock</a> (Enhanced Carbon) - $15-20 more per filter</p><ul><li>Double the activated carbon.</li><li>Perfect if you cook frequently or deal with smoke</li><li>Great for wildfire season</li><li>Same 6-9 month lifespan</li></ul><p><a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/products/allergenblock-replacement-filter-for-311i-max\">AllergenBlock</a> (Premium) - $20-25 more per filter</p><ul><li>Extra layers for allergy and asthma sufferers</li><li>Makes a real difference during pollen season</li><li>Investment in better sleep and fewer symptoms</li></ul><p>Subscription advantage: Upgrade to AllergenBlock during spring pollen, switch back to standard filters when needed. Bulk purchasing locks you into one choice for years, which rarely matches your actual needs throughout the seasons.</p><h2>How Filter Replacement Frequency Affects Your Subscription Decision</h2><p>Blueair's standard is 6-9 months, but your home determines the actual lifespan:</p><ul><li>9-12 months: Quiet area, no pets, low pollution</li><li>6-9 months: One or two pets, regular cooking, moderate pollution</li><li>3-6 months: Multiple pets, frequent cooking, high-pollution urban area</li></ul><p>Check your unit's indicator light; it tells you when replacement is actually needed, not calendar dates. This is exactly why automatic filter subscriptions make sense: you can't predict perfectly, so paying only for filters you actually use beats forecasting.</p><h2>Choosing Between Air Filter Subscriptions and Bulk: What Works for You</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
