        "text_Ub47yL": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-md",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-md",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-lg",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Choose a filter subscription if:</p><ul><li>You have multiple Blueair units to manage.</li><li>Life might change (new pet, moving, family growth)</li><li>You want flexibility and convenience.</li><li>You prefer small, regular payments over a bulk upfront.</li><li>You travel frequently</li></ul><p>Choose bulk if:</p><ul><li>One unit in stable conditions</li><li>You have climate-controlled storage.</li><li>Your household won't change in 3+ years.</li><li>You genuinely prefer upfront purchases.</li><li>You've calculated the exact needs.</li></ul><p>Honest truth: For most households, subscriptions win due to flexibility, not just cost. That peace of mind is worth $15-25 extra annually.</p><h2>Why Blueair Filters Matter for Your Air Purifier</h2><p>You might wonder if it is generic. Here's the critical difference: Blueair uses HEPASilent™ technology, combining mechanical and electrostatic filtration. Regular HEPA is mechanical only. Blueair's dual approach captures 99.97% of particles down to 0.1 microns, bacteria, viruses, pollen, dust, pet dander, and mold allergens.</p><p>Generic filters don't deliver the same performance because they're not engineered for electrostatic filtration. Blueair filters are specifically designed for this dual system. Using authentic Blueair filters ensures you're getting the performance you invested in.</p><p>With a filter subscription, you're guaranteed authentic Blueair filters every single time. No guessing, no compatibility worries, no wasted money.</p><h2>The Bottom Line: Filter Replacement Subscription or Bulk Purchase</h2><p>Is a filter subscription cheaper than buying in bulk? For stable single-unit homes, maybe $12-42 over three years. But those modest savings don't justify losing flexibility when life inevitably changes.</p><p>A filter subscription gives you:</p><ul><li>Guaranteed 15-20% savings on every filter</li><li>Flexibility to adjust as your life changes</li><li>Zero waste from incompatible filters</li><li>Convenience of automatic delivery</li><li>Peace of mind when circumstances shift</li></ul><p>For most people, that's worth far more than $15-25 extra yearly. Try a subscription for a few months. Experience the convenience. Most people find it's worth it.</p><h3>FAQs</h3><p><strong>Q. What's the actual discount with a Blueair filter subscription?</strong></p><p>25% off your first filter, then ongoing 15-20% savings on every replacement order.</p><p><strong>Q. Can I pause my air filter subscription whenever I need to?</strong></p><p>Yes, pause anytime without penalty. Resume whenever you need filters again.</p><p><strong>Q. Do Blueair filter subscriptions include free shipping?</strong></p><p>Yes, free shipping on all filter subscription orders is included in the service.</p><p><strong>Q. Which filter type should I choose for my filter subscription?</strong></p><p>Start with standard Particle + Carbon. Upgrade to SmokeBlock or AllergenBlock if needed.</p><p><strong>Q. How do I know when my filter actually needs replacement?</strong></p><p>Your unit's indicator light tells you when replacement is needed; don't guess with calendar dates.</p><p><strong>Q. Can I switch between filter types while subscribed?</strong></p><p>Yes, change types anytime. Upgrade during allergies, downgrade when conditions improve.</p><h3>Important Usage Information</h3><p>For optimal performance and safety, Blueair air purifiers are designed for indoor use in normal indoor environments. Do not use the appliance outdoors or in wet environments such as bathrooms, laundry rooms, or pool areas.</p><h3>About the Testing</h3><p>¹ Tested on bacteria (S. aureus, K. pneumoniae, P. aeruginosa), virus (MS2), and mold allergen (A. niger) with a minimum reduction rate of 99.9% in 60 minutes.</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
